# Keep the build context small and stable.
#
# Without this the context shipped ~63MB of generated files, including
# mobile/android/.gradle. A Gradle lock file in there was intermittently held by
# another process, which made the context transfer fail outright:
#
#   read mobile/android/.gradle/.../checksums.lock: The process cannot access
#   the file because another process has locked a portion of the file.
#
# Docker then reused the previous image, so a rebuild looked like it had
# succeeded while serving stale JavaScript.

.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store

# Flutter / Dart generated output
**/.dart_tool/
**/.packages
**/build/
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/.pub-cache/
**/.pub/

# Android build state. The app ships as web only, so none of this is needed to
# compile it, and .gradle in particular holds lock files.
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/app/build/
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/key.properties
**/*.iml

# Other platform folders: present for IDE convenience, unused by the web build.
mobile/ios/
mobile/linux/
mobile/macos/
mobile/windows/

# Editor noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp